# Hashed build assets are immutable: if one is missing, it is missing. Falling
# through to the SPA rule below would answer a .js request with index.html, and
# the browser rejects that with a MIME-type error that names neither the file
# nor the cause. This keeps that failure honest — and the app turns a failed
# chunk load into the "new version, reload" banner (see sw-update.ts).
/assets/*  /index.html  404

# SPA fallback: client-side routing serves index.html for any path that
# isn't a built asset, so deep links and reloads don't 404.
/*  /index.html  200
